1
00:00:02,070 --> 00:00:03,000
[Bayfront Metropolis]
No need to wait.

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:05,120
Chairman Yiu won't be able to make it today.

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:06,920
I look forward to a chance to work together in the future.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:07,790
Just

5
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,310
not on this project.

6
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:11,440
You mean Ascend is ending this partnership?

7
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:12,230
That's right.

8
00:00:12,230 --> 00:00:13,840
Has any one of your customers brought in

9
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:15,280
a motorbike for modification recently?

10
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:16,520
That guy said he'd just

11
00:00:16,680 --> 00:00:18,310
bought the bike and brought it in for modifications.

12
00:00:18,760 --> 00:00:20,470
But I could tell straight away it wasn't legit.

13
00:00:20,710 --> 00:00:23,360
I also heard him refer to himself

14
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:24,280
as K on the phone.

15
00:00:24,950 --> 00:00:25,760
What is this?

16
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:27,000
Our cigarette.

17
00:00:27,150 --> 00:00:28,760
What you've been dealing with lately

18
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:29,840
isn't against the law, is it?

19
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:31,600
Someone was being ungrateful.

20
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:32,710
I just taught him a lesson.

21
00:00:33,230 --> 00:00:34,710
Just be careful.

22
00:00:34,790 --> 00:00:36,150
I should be saying that to you.

23
00:00:36,390 --> 00:00:37,520
Be careful.

24
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:14,840
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

25
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:18,040
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

26
00:01:18,160 --> 00:01:20,950
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

27
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:23,380
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

28
00:01:23,520 --> 00:01:26,360
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

29
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:30,520
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

30
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:35,310
♪I'm willing to wait♪

31
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:39,000
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

32
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:41,800
♪I want to share my life with you♪

33
00:01:42,440 --> 00:01:48,220
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

34
00:01:48,570 --> 00:01:50,370
♪In this cold and gray city♪

35
00:01:50,450 --> 00:01:52,080
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

36
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,530
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

37
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:55,190
♪Stay with me♪

38
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:57,940
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

39
00:01:58,020 --> 00:01:58,720
♪Stay with me♪

40
00:01:58,800 --> 00:02:01,640
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

41
00:02:02,130 --> 00:02:04,140
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

42
00:02:04,670 --> 00:02:07,180
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

43
00:02:07,710 --> 00:02:10,220
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

44
00:02:10,940 --> 00:02:14,440
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

45
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:18,040
[Ash]
[Episode 4]

46
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:21,140
[Harbour Crystal Centre]

47
00:02:21,230 --> 00:02:22,390
Police of Hong Kong, China!

48
00:02:22,390 --> 00:02:24,520
We suspect someone on the premises is using counterfeit notes.

49
00:02:24,920 --> 00:02:27,000
We have a court-issued search warrant.

50
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Open the door immediately.

51
00:02:30,150 --> 00:02:30,920
Boss,

52
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,040
the police are outside.

53
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:36,840
Auntie Fan, about Uncle To,

54
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:37,760
we'll talk later.

55
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:38,710
Wait here for me.

56
00:02:41,230 --> 00:02:42,360
Routine police check.

57
00:02:42,760 --> 00:02:44,280
Everyone, get up and stand to the side.

58
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:45,920
Show your IDs.

59
00:02:46,040 --> 00:02:47,000
Officers,

60
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:48,870
how can I assist you?

61
00:02:49,310 --> 00:02:51,070
We're with the Commercial Crime Bureau.

62
00:02:51,680 --> 00:02:52,710
Are you in charge here?

63
00:02:53,070 --> 00:02:53,870
I am.

64
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,310
Here's the search warrant.

65
00:02:56,040 --> 00:02:58,230
We suspect someone here of using and possessing

66
00:02:58,230 --> 00:02:59,440
counterfeit notes.

67
00:03:00,390 --> 00:03:00,870
Go.

68
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:01,920
Take him in.

69
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,230
Mr. Hui,

70
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,600
please come with us to assist with our investigation.

71
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:09,790
Need a hood?

72
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,280
This is my turf.

73
00:03:12,630 --> 00:03:13,710
I've got nothing to fear.

74
00:03:16,470 --> 00:03:17,280
Look out!

75
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,440
You traitor!

76
00:03:33,710 --> 00:03:35,230
Joseph, call an ambulance.

77
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,470
Yes, sir.

78
00:03:36,870 --> 00:03:39,150
Shots fired. Someone's been hit. Send an ambulance.

79
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:42,420
[POLICE]

80
00:03:45,710 --> 00:03:47,000
Are you all right?

81
00:03:48,230 --> 00:03:49,950
Take everyone back to the station. We'll deal with it there!

82
00:03:52,920 --> 00:03:53,840
Come to the station with me.

83
00:04:39,520 --> 00:04:40,710
Mr. Hui Loek To,

84
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:43,710
do you admit that you run the casino?

85
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,440
I only own the premises.

86
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:48,310
Inviting friends over to watch a match

87
00:04:48,470 --> 00:04:49,760
isn't illegal, is it?

88
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:53,120
I'm the one asking the questions.

89
00:04:53,120 --> 00:04:54,310
You're not here to question me.

90
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:56,280
Please answer my questions

91
00:04:56,280 --> 00:04:58,950
truthfully and honestly.

92
00:04:59,390 --> 00:05:00,790
Don't try to hide anything.

93
00:05:01,070 --> 00:05:02,470
I've never been dishonest.

94
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,040
I've never lied to you.

95
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:07,630
You're hiding nothing?

96
00:05:08,630 --> 00:05:10,200
Then what's your connection to Dreamweaver?

97
00:05:10,310 --> 00:05:11,870
I don't know what Dreamweaver is.

98
00:05:11,920 --> 00:05:13,200
The currency counterfeiting syndicate!

99
00:05:14,070 --> 00:05:15,630
We already have evidence

100
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,920
that To Si Hong was involved in several major counterfeit money cases.

101
00:05:19,150 --> 00:05:21,680
And he was with Sheng Tung right up until he died.

102
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:22,680
Do you really have nothing to do with it?

103
00:05:22,680 --> 00:05:24,920
I couldn't control what To Si Hong did.

104
00:05:25,470 --> 00:05:27,000
If anything,

105
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:27,790
he was

106
00:05:27,790 --> 00:05:30,230
the perpetrator, and I was the victim.

107
00:05:30,470 --> 00:05:31,440
You're the victim?

108
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:32,390
Why can't I be the victim?

109
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:33,390
I told you not to answer with questions.

110
00:05:33,390 --> 00:05:34,630
Do you understand Chinese?

111
00:05:36,070 --> 00:05:37,440
Calm down first.

112
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:40,630
Once you piece everything together, you'll see I had nothing to do with it.

113
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:43,630
Did you know To Si Hong was

114
00:05:43,630 --> 00:05:45,440
colluding with other criminal organisations?

115
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:48,200
Is that why you hired someone to kill him?

116
00:05:52,550 --> 00:05:53,950
I've never killed anyone,

117
00:05:54,550 --> 00:05:56,470
and I've never hired anyone to kill him.

118
00:05:59,230 --> 00:06:00,150
You have to believe me.

119
00:06:02,760 --> 00:06:03,840
Believe you?

120
00:06:06,230 --> 00:06:07,840
You knew I was on the counterfeit money case.

121
00:06:08,310 --> 00:06:09,920
You knew I was investigating Sheng Tung.

122
00:06:10,230 --> 00:06:11,550
Yet you just stood by and watched.

123
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,230
Do you think I'm a fool?

124
00:06:13,710 --> 00:06:14,470
Fei Foon...

125
00:06:14,470 --> 00:06:15,280
Don't call me Fei Foon.

126
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:15,950
Call me Officer!

127
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,230
Officer,

128
00:06:30,760 --> 00:06:33,200
I don't think I need to tell you every detail of my private affairs.

129
00:06:39,360 --> 00:06:39,950
Officer Mok,

130
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:41,230
the Hui family's lawyer is here.

131
00:06:41,470 --> 00:06:42,630
He's been granted bail.

132
00:06:42,950 --> 00:06:44,390
Officer Chan says to release him now.

133
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:45,790
Mr. Hui, I'm sorry

134
00:06:45,790 --> 00:06:46,470
for being late.

135
00:06:47,230 --> 00:06:48,310
Did they try to coerce a confession?

136
00:06:50,120 --> 00:06:50,920
No.

137
00:06:51,870 --> 00:06:52,680
Officer,

138
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:54,870
all the bail formalities are complete.

139
00:06:55,070 --> 00:06:57,000
I require that my client be released immediately.

140
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:01,520
You think I want to see him?

141
00:07:02,120 --> 00:07:03,680
Please take him away right now.

142
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:05,600
Don't let him get in the way here.

143
00:07:06,230 --> 00:07:06,870
Go.

144
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:53,550
Officer Mok, are you all right?

145
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,120
Did you get hurt?

146
00:07:55,310 --> 00:07:56,390
It was so chaotic just now

147
00:07:56,550 --> 00:07:58,040
that I didn't have a chance to check on you.

148
00:07:58,840 --> 00:07:59,790
I'm fine. Don't worry.

149
00:08:00,120 --> 00:08:01,070
Good.

150
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:02,760
Now that K is dead,

151
00:08:03,150 --> 00:08:04,870
he won't be coming after you for revenge anymore.

152
00:08:05,040 --> 00:08:06,680
Every day, I worried he'd show up like last time

153
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,550
and try to hurt you.

154
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,710
Now I can finally relax.

155
00:08:10,230 --> 00:08:11,390
Since you're safe and sound,

156
00:08:11,760 --> 00:08:13,230
how about we have a nice dinner tonight?

157
00:08:13,230 --> 00:08:13,790
My treat.

158
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:15,680
No, thanks.

159
00:08:15,680 --> 00:08:16,920
I want to be alone.

160
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:19,680
All right.

161
00:08:20,150 --> 00:08:22,440
Take some time to yourself and get some rest.

162
00:08:22,790 --> 00:08:24,630
Call me anytime if anything happens.

163
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:25,440
Okay.

164
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,520
I'll get going.

165
00:08:36,130 --> 00:08:38,430
[Maybe decadence is another kind of beauty]

166
00:08:41,770 --> 00:08:43,100
[To]

167
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,150
Sir.

168
00:08:52,230 --> 00:08:53,280
The usual?

169
00:08:53,710 --> 00:08:54,680
Sure. Thanks.

170
00:09:08,040 --> 00:09:09,040
Excuse me.

171
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:11,760
There are plenty of empty tables.

172
00:09:11,760 --> 00:09:13,440
You don't need to share mine.

173
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:14,870
Could you sit somewhere else?

174
00:09:15,440 --> 00:09:16,230
Fei Foon?

175
00:09:17,470 --> 00:09:18,280
Who are you?

176
00:09:19,070 --> 00:09:19,870
Foon Gor, right?

177
00:09:21,310 --> 00:09:22,200
Shawn?

178
00:09:22,230 --> 00:09:23,040
It really is you.

179
00:09:26,840 --> 00:09:28,520
I knew you wouldn't forget me.

180
00:09:35,070 --> 00:09:35,790
All right.

181
00:09:37,150 --> 00:09:37,710
Let's sit.

182
00:09:37,710 --> 00:09:38,230
All right.

183
00:09:41,520 --> 00:09:42,920
We haven't seen each other in years

184
00:09:42,920 --> 00:09:44,120
since I moved away.

185
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:45,040
Where have you been?

186
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:47,230
I went to study in the UK.

187
00:09:48,520 --> 00:09:49,870
I only returned to Hong Kong, China recently.

188
00:09:50,150 --> 00:09:51,680
I started looking for you as soon as I got back,

189
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:53,230
but I could never find you.

190
00:09:54,040 --> 00:09:56,470
Who would've thought? I ran into you today at a restaurant.

191
00:09:56,920 --> 00:09:58,230
Guess we were meant to meet again.

192
00:09:59,550 --> 00:10:00,520
Definitely.

193
00:10:00,710 --> 00:10:01,840
Let's order first.

194
00:10:02,760 --> 00:10:04,040
My family was too poor back then.

195
00:10:05,040 --> 00:10:06,550
I could never eat the food I craved.

196
00:10:08,040 --> 00:10:09,310
Now I'm going to eat my fill.

197
00:10:09,310 --> 00:10:10,200
Sir.

198
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:11,280
Yes, just a moment.

199
00:10:12,550 --> 00:10:13,360
What would you like?

200
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:16,230
What are you having?

201
00:10:16,390 --> 00:10:16,790
I know.

202
00:10:17,470 --> 00:10:18,950
I'll have the crispy bun with condensed milk.

203
00:10:18,950 --> 00:10:19,360
Okay.

204
00:10:19,870 --> 00:10:20,600
Red bean ice.

205
00:10:20,790 --> 00:10:21,200
Okay.

206
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:21,920
And fried chicken wings.

207
00:10:22,040 --> 00:10:22,600
Okay.

208
00:10:22,950 --> 00:10:24,280
And a buttered pineapple bun.

209
00:10:24,280 --> 00:10:25,040
Buttered pineapple bun.

210
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:25,920
Two of each.

211
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:26,630
Two of everything?

212
00:10:26,630 --> 00:10:27,390
Yes.

213
00:10:27,390 --> 00:10:28,310
Okay, sure.

214
00:10:28,710 --> 00:10:29,520
Please wait a moment.

215
00:10:35,280 --> 00:10:36,070
Enjoy.

216
00:10:45,710 --> 00:10:46,840
Let's eat.

217
00:10:56,470 --> 00:10:57,680
Since coming back,

218
00:10:58,310 --> 00:11:00,440
I feel like Hong Kong, China hasn't changed much all these years.

219
00:11:01,310 --> 00:11:02,310
It's still so stifling.

220
00:11:04,920 --> 00:11:05,710
Not really.

221
00:11:06,470 --> 00:11:07,760
A lot has changed.

222
00:11:08,630 --> 00:11:09,870
You only just got back.

223
00:11:09,870 --> 00:11:10,680
You just haven't noticed.

224
00:11:10,870 --> 00:11:11,680
I don't think so.

225
00:11:12,870 --> 00:11:14,760
You haven't changed at all, Foon Gor.

226
00:11:15,710 --> 00:11:18,120
You're exactly the same as when we were kids.

227
00:11:19,710 --> 00:11:20,520
I still remember.

228
00:11:23,070 --> 00:11:23,950
I still remember

229
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:25,870
everything you did for me

230
00:11:26,040 --> 00:11:27,390
back then.

231
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:29,630
I also remember

232
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:30,950
I swore

233
00:11:31,950 --> 00:11:32,760
that in this life,

234
00:11:33,230 --> 00:11:34,440
I'd always stay with you,

235
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:35,520
and we'd never be apart again.

236
00:11:35,710 --> 00:11:36,120
Hey.

237
00:11:36,870 --> 00:11:39,120
That's a pretty serious vow for a kid.

238
00:11:40,280 --> 00:11:41,280
Looking back,

239
00:11:41,870 --> 00:11:43,230
we really would say anything when we were kids.

240
00:11:44,520 --> 00:11:49,070
But as I recall, didn't your father...?

241
00:11:50,070 --> 00:11:50,920
It's okay.

242
00:11:52,600 --> 00:11:54,150
You can say it.

243
00:11:55,870 --> 00:11:57,150
It's all in the past.

244
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:00,040
Back then,

245
00:12:00,920 --> 00:12:02,710
my dad would often get drunk and beat me.

246
00:12:03,630 --> 00:12:04,630
He was brutal.

247
00:12:06,950 --> 00:12:09,790
You little brat, how dare you disobey me!

248
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:20,150
You little brat, how dare you disobey me!

249
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:29,720
You were the first person who came to save me.

250
00:12:30,440 --> 00:12:31,480
You were amazing.

251
00:12:32,150 --> 00:12:32,870
Come on!

252
00:12:32,870 --> 00:12:34,040
You little brat!

253
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:36,000
If you've got the guts, don't come back!

254
00:13:07,550 --> 00:13:08,360
Hurry up and eat.

255
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:09,470
Put something in your stomach.

256
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:10,870
I know you're hungry.

257
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:12,390
Thanks.

258
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:20,550
Silly,

259
00:13:20,550 --> 00:13:21,360
no need to thank me.

260
00:13:22,040 --> 00:13:24,000
If he hurts you again next time,

261
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:25,390
remember to come find me.

262
00:13:29,360 --> 00:13:30,600
We'll fight back together.

263
00:13:31,150 --> 00:13:32,630
We'll hit him back

264
00:13:33,550 --> 00:13:36,630
so he won't dare to hurt you anymore.

265
00:13:41,840 --> 00:13:42,630
Okay.

266
00:13:43,280 --> 00:13:44,630
But even when I'm not around,

267
00:13:48,390 --> 00:13:50,230
you have to protect yourself.

268
00:13:51,070 --> 00:13:51,950
Got it?

269
00:13:55,550 --> 00:13:56,440
Got it.

270
00:13:58,000 --> 00:13:58,750
Back then,

271
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,270
you only had enough money for one pineapple bun,

272
00:14:01,270 --> 00:14:02,550
but you still bought it for me.

273
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,750
You told me not to be afraid

274
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,270
and said

275
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:08,390
you'd always look out for me.

276
00:14:18,470 --> 00:14:19,440
I'm not exaggerating.

277
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,280
Back then,

278
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:23,120
you really saved my life.

279
00:14:23,840 --> 00:14:25,280
Why bring all this up as soon as we meet again?

280
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,280
I was just recklessly brave back then.

281
00:14:28,950 --> 00:14:30,550
Later, a couple

282
00:14:31,390 --> 00:14:32,550
adopted me

283
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,360
and took me to the UK with them.

284
00:14:37,040 --> 00:14:39,000
I'm glad you found people who looked out for you.

285
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:39,870
Enough about that.

286
00:14:39,870 --> 00:14:41,000
Let's eat.

287
00:14:41,280 --> 00:14:42,070
The food's getting cold.

288
00:14:43,360 --> 00:14:44,790
I'm not actually that hungry.

289
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:47,000
I only came here to sit for a while.

290
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:49,950
That's okay.

291
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:51,870
Just eat what you can.

292
00:15:02,230 --> 00:15:03,070
Full?

293
00:15:03,070 --> 00:15:04,000
If you are, let's go.

294
00:15:04,200 --> 00:15:05,000
Let's go.

295
00:15:07,070 --> 00:15:07,760
I'll pay.

296
00:15:09,150 --> 00:15:10,550
Kid, don't fight me for the bill.

297
00:15:11,390 --> 00:15:12,200
Don't be silly.

298
00:15:12,280 --> 00:15:13,280
I ordered the food.

299
00:15:13,280 --> 00:15:14,000
Of course I'm paying.

300
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:15,950
Foon Gor, wait outside for me.

301
00:15:16,150 --> 00:15:16,790
Sir.

302
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:17,760
Coming.

303
00:15:20,280 --> 00:15:21,200
How much is it?

304
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:22,040
One moment.

305
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:27,550
Fei Foon.

306
00:15:27,980 --> 00:15:30,990
[May Business Prosper]

307
00:15:31,550 --> 00:15:33,120
Calm down and hear me out.

308
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:33,870
About To Si Hong...

309
00:15:33,870 --> 00:15:34,550
What?

310
00:15:34,630 --> 00:15:35,630
What do you want to say?

311
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:37,200
Think carefully.

312
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:39,150
Your lawyer isn't here now.

313
00:15:39,950 --> 00:15:40,600
With that attitude,

314
00:15:40,600 --> 00:15:41,680
we can't communicate.

315
00:15:41,680 --> 00:15:42,790
What attitude?

316
00:15:43,600 --> 00:15:45,760
Unless you tell me who killed To Si Hong,

317
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:48,120
I don't want to hear anything else.

318
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,680
Do you really think I killed him?

319
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:53,310
I don't know.

320
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,230
Right now, I don't even know who you really are.

321
00:15:56,520 --> 00:15:57,760
I know you're angry.

322
00:15:57,760 --> 00:15:58,760
I've been looking everywhere for you.

323
00:15:58,760 --> 00:16:00,040
Isn't that enough?

324
00:16:03,070 --> 00:16:03,870
Foon Gor.

325
00:16:05,760 --> 00:16:06,790
Is this your friend?

326
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:08,790
I don't know him.

327
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:09,950
Let's go.

328
00:16:13,020 --> 00:16:13,860
It's you?

329
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,360
Hello, I can't take your call right now.

330
00:16:31,550 --> 00:16:32,030
If you...

331
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,360
Loek To, are you ready?

332
00:16:46,360 --> 00:16:47,390
We need to get going.

333
00:16:59,550 --> 00:17:00,440
Let's go.

334
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:05,680
[Bayfront Metropolis Construction]
Now, the highlight of the event.

335
00:17:05,710 --> 00:17:08,600
[Phase One Launching Ceremony]
Tin Ping Group previously commissioned

336
00:17:08,600 --> 00:17:10,280
Stanley University to conduct a comprehensive

337
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:12,360
environmental assessment of the Bayfront Metropolis project.

338
00:17:12,920 --> 00:17:15,120
It received the highest rating, Grade A,

339
00:17:15,120 --> 00:17:16,710
meaning the project can now proceed

340
00:17:16,710 --> 00:17:18,230
with preliminary work for phase one.

341
00:17:18,390 --> 00:17:19,470
Today, we are honoured to have

342
00:17:19,470 --> 00:17:20,920
the Director of Environmental Protection,

343
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:22,360
Mr. Wong Tak Kuen,

344
00:17:22,360 --> 00:17:23,080
join us

345
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:25,870
at this simple yet formal launching ceremony.

346
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:26,710
Ready?

347
00:17:26,710 --> 00:17:28,280
- Three, two... - Get out of my way!

348
00:17:28,280 --> 00:17:29,680
Hui Loek To, you hypocrite!

349
00:17:29,680 --> 00:17:30,470
You're a fraud!

350
00:17:31,600 --> 00:17:32,360
Do you know

351
00:17:32,360 --> 00:17:34,000
the funding for Tin Ping Group's landscaping project

352
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,230
is all dirty money?

353
00:17:35,310 --> 00:17:36,390
Because I found out,

354
00:17:36,390 --> 00:17:37,710
you had people beat me up

355
00:17:37,710 --> 00:17:38,870
and hold me against my will.

356
00:17:38,870 --> 00:17:39,870
He pretends to be a saint,

357
00:17:40,030 --> 00:17:41,030
doing charity everywhere.

358
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:42,360
But in fact, it's all an act!

359
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:43,920
He paints himself as an honest businessman,

360
00:17:43,920 --> 00:17:45,550
but he's really a gangster!

361
00:17:46,950 --> 00:17:47,520
Out of my way!

362
00:17:47,520 --> 00:17:49,150
Sir, I'd like to ask you something.

363
00:17:49,150 --> 00:17:50,230
Do you have evidence

364
00:17:50,230 --> 00:17:52,360
that Mr. Hui Loek To had you severely beaten?

365
00:17:52,630 --> 00:17:53,550
And as for your claim

366
00:17:53,550 --> 00:17:55,470
that Tin Ping Group's project is funded with dirty money,

367
00:17:55,470 --> 00:17:57,080
do you have any concrete evidence?

368
00:17:57,390 --> 00:17:59,080
Mr. Hui, do you know this man?

369
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,470
Is what he's saying true?

370
00:18:00,470 --> 00:18:02,950
Is this project funded entirely with dirty money?

371
00:18:02,950 --> 00:18:05,150
Do you secretly run illegal businesses linked to organised crime?

372
00:18:05,230 --> 00:18:06,550
Please respond. Thank you.

373
00:18:06,630 --> 00:18:07,710
Chairman Hui, regarding these allegations,

374
00:18:07,710 --> 00:18:09,030
do you have anything to say?

375
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:10,030
Let go of me!

376
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:11,310
Hui Loek To!

377
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:13,760
I'm settling this with you today!

378
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:14,550
Stay out of this!

379
00:18:19,710 --> 00:18:20,870
Avoiding the questions won't solve anything,

380
00:18:20,870 --> 00:18:21,310
Mr. Hui.

381
00:18:21,630 --> 00:18:22,470
Everyone saw that!

382
00:18:22,470 --> 00:18:23,200
He assaulted me!

383
00:18:23,520 --> 00:18:25,470
His brother is in on it with him.

384
00:18:25,470 --> 00:18:26,840
They're both gangsters!

385
00:18:27,360 --> 00:18:28,550
I'm calling the police.

386
00:18:28,550 --> 00:18:30,000
I'm going to sue the whole Hui family.

387
00:18:30,080 --> 00:18:31,630
I'll sue them until they lose everything!

388
00:18:33,020 --> 00:18:35,440
[Sham Shui Po Police Station]

389
00:18:37,520 --> 00:18:39,870
If you won't cooperate, you can keep sitting there.

390
00:18:39,870 --> 00:18:42,950
You can't leave until the 48 hours are up.

391
00:18:47,080 --> 00:18:47,870
On.

392
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:50,710
That man is a real handful.

393
00:18:51,080 --> 00:18:51,870
What happened?

394
00:18:51,870 --> 00:18:53,470
He barged into Tin Ping Group's event and accused

395
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:54,870
the chairman of involvement in organised crime,

396
00:18:54,870 --> 00:18:56,360
false imprisonment and assault.

397
00:18:56,470 --> 00:18:57,470
But once he got to the station,

398
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:58,360
he wouldn't say a word.

399
00:18:58,360 --> 00:18:59,230
He wouldn't get a lawyer either.

400
00:18:59,470 --> 00:19:00,760
He refuses to talk unless the media are around,

401
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:02,470
like we're the ones out to get him.

402
00:19:02,950 --> 00:19:04,360
What exactly is he trying to do?

403
00:19:04,390 --> 00:19:05,760
Is he only after media attention?

404
00:19:06,280 --> 00:19:08,550
Who knows? Either way, he's a real headache.

405
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,470
The younger Mr. Hui, however,

406
00:19:10,470 --> 00:19:12,390
has been surprisingly cooperative.

407
00:19:12,470 --> 00:19:13,310
He answered every question.

408
00:19:15,230 --> 00:19:16,440
That's unexpected.

409
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:18,000
I'll get back to work.

410
00:19:34,790 --> 00:19:35,470
Mr. Hui,

411
00:19:35,470 --> 00:19:36,310
please wait here

412
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:37,080
while I finish the formalities.

413
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:38,630
Mr. Choi, this way, please.

414
00:19:59,630 --> 00:20:03,230
You're Hui Loek To's younger brother, Hui Luk King, right?

415
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:05,120
Yes. Hello,

416
00:20:05,950 --> 00:20:06,760
Officer Mok.

417
00:20:08,030 --> 00:20:12,120
I heard you pushed Mr. Wong off the stage this afternoon

418
00:20:12,310 --> 00:20:13,310
and injured him.

419
00:20:13,310 --> 00:20:14,230
Is that true?

420
00:20:15,230 --> 00:20:17,440
It was chaotic at the time.

421
00:20:18,390 --> 00:20:21,280
I was worried he'd hurt my brother,

422
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:23,870
so I stepped in to separate them

423
00:20:23,870 --> 00:20:25,470
and accidentally pushed him to the ground.

424
00:20:26,470 --> 00:20:28,120
Is he all right?

425
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:30,120
You really are brothers.

426
00:20:30,120 --> 00:20:31,120
You're both great actors.

427
00:20:31,470 --> 00:20:33,230
You know my brother?

428
00:20:34,870 --> 00:20:36,950
I don't know if I really know him.

429
00:20:37,920 --> 00:20:39,520
Anyway, the Hui family

430
00:20:39,630 --> 00:20:42,790
are legitimate business people at Tin Ping Group on the surface,

431
00:20:43,630 --> 00:20:46,120
but behind the scenes, you run the shady Sheng Tung.

432
00:20:46,630 --> 00:20:47,870
Tell me the truth.

433
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:51,230
What other illegal things has your brother been involved in?

434
00:20:54,950 --> 00:20:58,360
You're the officer who's been giving my brother such a hard time.

435
00:20:59,600 --> 00:21:00,390
He

436
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:02,230
mentioned me to you?

437
00:21:02,630 --> 00:21:03,470
No.

438
00:21:03,630 --> 00:21:06,000
I heard about you from Fung.

439
00:21:09,470 --> 00:21:10,440
I'm glad you're here.

440
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,520
There's something I wanted to tell you.

441
00:21:13,790 --> 00:21:14,600
Go ahead.

442
00:21:16,760 --> 00:21:17,550
Officer Mok,

443
00:21:17,600 --> 00:21:21,080
I think you know our family background is fairly complicated.

444
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:23,440
Ever since our father passed away,

445
00:21:23,760 --> 00:21:26,360
my brother had to learn how to take over the family businesses,

446
00:21:27,150 --> 00:21:28,360
what he should do,

447
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:30,080
what he shouldn't do,

448
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:31,840
and how to negotiate with people

449
00:21:31,840 --> 00:21:33,600
without revealing what he really thought.

450
00:21:35,150 --> 00:21:36,360
At the end of the day,

451
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:37,390
the more you say,

452
00:21:37,390 --> 00:21:38,840
the more likely you are to expose your weaknesses.

453
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:40,550
What does any of that have to do with me?

454
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:43,920
Fung told me that at the casino last time,

455
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:46,760
my brother had countless chances to get out clean

456
00:21:46,870 --> 00:21:48,440
and keep everything hidden from you,

457
00:21:48,440 --> 00:21:51,080
but he chose not to.

458
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,360
So because he saved me,

459
00:21:54,360 --> 00:21:56,030
I'm supposed to accept his grey-area dealings,

460
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:57,870
the fact that he hides things from me,

461
00:21:58,440 --> 00:22:00,230
and all the illegal things he does?

462
00:22:01,680 --> 00:22:02,790
What I'm saying is,

463
00:22:03,550 --> 00:22:05,440
after you came into his life,

464
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:09,000
he no longer cared only about the family's interests.

465
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:11,790
He doesn't even put his own safety first anymore.

466
00:22:15,600 --> 00:22:17,000
Actually,

467
00:22:17,390 --> 00:22:18,600
whether you forgive him or not

468
00:22:18,600 --> 00:22:19,600
isn't for me to interfere with.

469
00:22:19,710 --> 00:22:20,790
It's just

470
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:24,150
that no one in our world has complete freedom of choice,

471
00:22:24,310 --> 00:22:25,520
especially not my brother.

472
00:22:25,630 --> 00:22:26,790
He's in a position

473
00:22:27,310 --> 00:22:29,080
of great responsibility.

474
00:22:29,310 --> 00:22:30,310
There are many things

475
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:32,000
he simply can't decide for himself.

476
00:22:32,840 --> 00:22:34,680
What kind of responsibility has to be shouldered

477
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:37,200
through shady dealings and illegal business?

478
00:22:37,520 --> 00:22:38,230
Seriously?

479
00:22:38,840 --> 00:22:41,230
Are you telling me how tough it is to be rich right now?

480
00:22:42,080 --> 00:22:42,840
Officer Mok,

481
00:22:42,950 --> 00:22:44,840
haven't you ever had to make

482
00:22:44,840 --> 00:22:46,600
a difficult choice because of your job?

483
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:47,680
What do you mean by that?

484
00:22:48,280 --> 00:22:49,840
Are you saying I'd break the law too?

485
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:52,920
No, that's not what I mean.

486
00:22:53,840 --> 00:22:56,120
I'm just trying to tell you

487
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:57,600
that my brother

488
00:22:57,840 --> 00:23:00,550
only shows people what he wants them to see.

489
00:23:00,950 --> 00:23:02,630
He's like that even with me.

490
00:23:02,790 --> 00:23:05,600
Maybe it's because he's guarded,

491
00:23:05,870 --> 00:23:07,080
or maybe he doesn't want to cause more trouble.

492
00:23:09,360 --> 00:23:12,950
Only he knows the real reason.

493
00:23:16,710 --> 00:23:18,230
I know he's under pressure.

494
00:23:19,550 --> 00:23:21,080
But no matter how little choice he has,

495
00:23:22,470 --> 00:23:24,710
at the very least, he should be honest with me.

496
00:23:26,470 --> 00:23:27,790
Honest?

497
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:30,550
Asking him to be honest

498
00:23:30,550 --> 00:23:33,440
is like making him abandon what he's relied on to survive all these years.

499
00:23:33,710 --> 00:23:34,630
The consequences could be even worse.

500
00:23:35,360 --> 00:23:36,150
But I can't stand

501
00:23:36,150 --> 00:23:37,710
being with someone who always hides things from me.

502
00:23:39,310 --> 00:23:39,950
I understand.

503
00:23:39,950 --> 00:23:41,710
That's up to you.

504
00:23:42,710 --> 00:23:43,360
But

505
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:47,520
as much as I worry that my brother

506
00:23:47,550 --> 00:23:49,550
will act without regard for his own safety,

507
00:23:49,790 --> 00:23:50,870
I haven't

508
00:23:52,310 --> 00:23:54,030
seen him smile so genuinely

509
00:23:54,030 --> 00:23:56,550
in a very long time.

510
00:23:59,130 --> 00:23:59,940
Anyway,

511
00:24:00,740 --> 00:24:02,370
while he may seem successful

512
00:24:02,660 --> 00:24:04,500
and capable of anything in the business world,

513
00:24:05,100 --> 00:24:07,340
getting him to open up

514
00:24:07,370 --> 00:24:09,100
and say what he really feels is

515
00:24:09,310 --> 00:24:10,630
something I can't begin to imagine.

516
00:24:11,230 --> 00:24:12,950
Why don't I leave that to you?

517
00:24:13,120 --> 00:24:14,950
Sit him down and make him have a proper talk with you.

518
00:24:15,150 --> 00:24:17,390
Maybe he'll be willing to open up to you.

519
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:19,950
You think I want a talk with him?

520
00:24:20,360 --> 00:24:21,630
What he thinks has nothing to do with me.

521
00:24:23,920 --> 00:24:24,870
All right, Officer Mok.

522
00:24:24,870 --> 00:24:26,030
Whatever you say.

523
00:24:28,920 --> 00:24:31,150
Officer Mok, what are you doing here?

524
00:24:31,310 --> 00:24:32,000
Well,

525
00:24:32,120 --> 00:24:33,000
I had a few words with him.

526
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:39,950
Mr. Hui,

527
00:24:40,150 --> 00:24:41,440
all the paperwork has been completed.

528
00:24:41,630 --> 00:24:42,600
You may leave now.

529
00:25:07,550 --> 00:25:08,200
Siu Kit.

530
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:10,680
Do you have Hui Loek To's file ready?

531
00:25:11,080 --> 00:25:12,710
It's right here.

532
00:25:13,200 --> 00:25:14,150
Give me a moment.

533
00:25:17,790 --> 00:25:18,600
Here's everything.

534
00:25:20,780 --> 00:25:23,260
[Property Tycoon Shot Dead in Suspected Gang Dispute]

535
00:25:23,290 --> 00:25:24,420
[Gang Infighting: Leader Likely Killed by Associate]

536
00:25:26,950 --> 00:25:28,000
That's it?

537
00:25:28,950 --> 00:25:30,760
Wasn't Sheng Tung a fairly large operation?

538
00:25:31,080 --> 00:25:31,760
That's it.

539
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:34,710
Sheng Tung was built up by two elders of the Hui family.

540
00:25:34,920 --> 00:25:36,230
They were powerful in the early days.

541
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:37,950
But after an internal power struggle,

542
00:25:38,200 --> 00:25:40,710
Old Mr. Hui was ousted and stripped of power by Sheng Tung's senior members,

543
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:41,630
and Sheng Tung declined sharply.

544
00:25:42,200 --> 00:25:45,000
His two sons don't have much influence now.

545
00:25:48,790 --> 00:25:49,600
Thanks.

546
00:25:49,600 --> 00:25:50,310
No problem.

547
00:25:50,310 --> 00:25:50,920
I'll get back to work.

548
00:26:08,840 --> 00:26:12,680
[Do you have time to meet?]

549
00:26:19,750 --> 00:26:21,630
[Police Station]

550
00:26:21,650 --> 00:26:23,200
[Sham Shui Po Police Station]

551
00:26:23,230 --> 00:26:26,120
The police didn't give you a hard time, did they?

552
00:26:26,550 --> 00:26:27,360
No.

553
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:28,310
They just took my statement.

554
00:26:28,950 --> 00:26:31,710
I heard from an officer that Mr. Wong isn't planning to press charges.

555
00:26:32,440 --> 00:26:33,310
That's unusual.

556
00:26:34,230 --> 00:26:36,150
I'll have Fung look into why he suddenly came to cause trouble

557
00:26:36,150 --> 00:26:37,230
and then backed off just as suddenly.

558
00:26:38,680 --> 00:26:40,310
Has Director Wong said anything?

559
00:26:41,440 --> 00:26:42,550
Director Wong

560
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:46,030
now has concerns about Tin Ping Group.

561
00:26:46,790 --> 00:26:49,150
The environmental assessment report will have to wait until the police

562
00:26:49,150 --> 00:26:50,360
complete their investigation

563
00:26:50,360 --> 00:26:52,200
before it can proceed as originally planned.

564
00:26:52,920 --> 00:26:53,710
It can't be expedited.

565
00:26:55,550 --> 00:26:57,950
So how long will the Bayfront Metropolis project be delayed?

566
00:26:58,310 --> 00:26:59,840
That depends on how quickly the investigation goes.

567
00:27:02,950 --> 00:27:04,310
What's wrong? Are you okay?

568
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:07,950
The investors said they needed

569
00:27:07,950 --> 00:27:09,920
to reassess whether they still wanted to invest.

570
00:27:09,920 --> 00:27:10,760
What should we do?

571
00:27:11,390 --> 00:27:12,600
That's nothing major.

572
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:15,470
Your top priority now is to get some rest.

573
00:27:15,470 --> 00:27:17,000
Deal with tomorrow's problems tomorrow.

574
00:27:17,710 --> 00:27:18,470
Okay?

575
00:27:18,470 --> 00:27:19,310
Okay.

576
00:27:19,310 --> 00:27:20,360
The car's up ahead.

577
00:27:20,360 --> 00:27:20,710
Let's go.

578
00:27:28,360 --> 00:27:31,920
[Do you have time to meet?]

579
00:27:35,390 --> 00:27:36,200
Something came up.

580
00:27:36,200 --> 00:27:37,030
You go back first.

581
00:27:37,230 --> 00:27:38,030
Drive.

582
00:27:58,230 --> 00:27:59,030
Fei Foon.

583
00:28:14,790 --> 00:28:16,000
I had nothing to do with the counterfeit notes.

584
00:28:19,310 --> 00:28:20,710
I didn't send anyone to beat up Mr. Wong.

585
00:28:22,390 --> 00:28:23,760
I didn't kill To Si Hong.

586
00:28:26,840 --> 00:28:28,310
I don't care what the rumours say.

587
00:28:29,150 --> 00:28:30,520
If I didn't do it, I didn't do it.

588
00:28:35,630 --> 00:28:38,950
Why didn't you ever tell me about your organised crime background?

589
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:45,630
Are you trying to turn Tin Ping into a criminal organisation?

590
00:28:47,310 --> 00:28:48,150
Of course not.

591
00:28:49,230 --> 00:28:51,440
Then why are you involved with those people?

592
00:28:53,360 --> 00:28:54,710
Doesn't the police force

593
00:28:55,760 --> 00:28:57,120
have a file on Sheng Tung?

594
00:28:58,440 --> 00:28:59,710
I want to hear it from you.

595
00:29:22,600 --> 00:29:23,710
Can you play basketball?

596
00:29:24,550 --> 00:29:25,390
I can, a little.

597
00:29:26,200 --> 00:29:27,390
Let's make a bet.

598
00:29:28,120 --> 00:29:29,310
Teach me how to play.

599
00:29:29,950 --> 00:29:32,920
If I can make a three-pointer tonight,

600
00:29:32,920 --> 00:29:34,120
I won't ask any more questions.

601
00:29:34,790 --> 00:29:37,030
But if I don't make a single one all night,

602
00:29:37,120 --> 00:29:38,280
you have to tell me the truth

603
00:29:38,280 --> 00:29:39,790
about why you're involved with those people.

604
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:40,470
Deal?

605
00:29:41,120 --> 00:29:42,710
A three-pointer's too hard.

606
00:29:42,710 --> 00:29:43,550
Make it a free throw.

607
00:29:43,950 --> 00:29:44,870
Are you teaching me or not?

608
00:29:45,470 --> 00:29:46,200
Come on.

609
00:29:51,870 --> 00:29:52,760
Here.

610
00:30:14,630 --> 00:30:15,470
Look.

611
00:30:16,600 --> 00:30:18,030
Shooting is easy.

612
00:30:18,440 --> 00:30:20,030
"Your left hand is only there to guide the ball."

613
00:30:20,200 --> 00:30:21,030
Ever heard that before?

614
00:30:22,030 --> 00:30:23,470
Shoot it like this.

615
00:30:24,710 --> 00:30:25,520
You try.

616
00:30:28,030 --> 00:30:28,870
Like this.

617
00:30:28,870 --> 00:30:29,920
Hold the ball properly.

618
00:30:31,630 --> 00:30:32,230
That's it.

619
00:30:33,120 --> 00:30:34,150
Grip it from above.

620
00:30:35,360 --> 00:30:36,150
Push with your middle finger.

621
00:30:38,000 --> 00:30:38,790
Raise it up

622
00:30:40,630 --> 00:30:41,630
and release from here.

623
00:30:43,120 --> 00:30:44,280
Let's put the ball down first.

624
00:30:45,950 --> 00:30:46,840
Feet apart.

625
00:30:48,310 --> 00:30:48,840
That's right.

626
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:49,920
Now bend your knees slightly.

627
00:30:51,630 --> 00:30:52,630
When I say, "Ready, three, two, one,"

628
00:30:52,630 --> 00:30:53,680
shoot the ball upwards.

629
00:30:54,630 --> 00:30:55,630
All right. Ready?

630
00:30:55,630 --> 00:30:57,550
Three, two, one.

631
00:31:04,630 --> 00:31:05,630
- Go get the ball. - You get it.

632
00:31:42,760 --> 00:31:44,030
Do you think this one will go in?

633
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:45,030
Yeah.

634
00:31:52,150 --> 00:31:53,150
Normally, I'd make that shot.

635
00:31:53,920 --> 00:31:54,710
Get the ball for me.

636
00:31:55,550 --> 00:31:56,360
I'm not getting it.

637
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:06,630
So,

638
00:32:07,630 --> 00:32:09,080
why are you involved in shady dealings?

639
00:32:09,470 --> 00:32:10,280
Does it really matter?

640
00:32:10,760 --> 00:32:12,470
If it didn't, I wouldn't keep asking.

641
00:32:16,390 --> 00:32:17,870
It goes back a long way.

642
00:32:19,920 --> 00:32:22,760
Both my parents started out as gangsters.

643
00:32:25,000 --> 00:32:27,120
They founded Tin Ping only to go legit.

644
00:32:28,470 --> 00:32:30,440
A lot of the older generation got involved back then,

645
00:32:31,360 --> 00:32:33,950
and those ties have carried on to this day.

646
00:32:37,030 --> 00:32:38,840
Can't you just pay them to leave?

647
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:40,790
They're all in it for the money anyway.

648
00:32:41,280 --> 00:32:42,520
It's not that simple.

649
00:32:43,120 --> 00:32:44,360
Have you tried?

650
00:32:55,470 --> 00:32:56,680
My dad did.

651
00:32:59,920 --> 00:33:00,710
Hui,

652
00:33:01,790 --> 00:33:03,200
now that you've made it,

653
00:33:03,870 --> 00:33:06,080
you don't care what happens to us anymore, do you?

654
00:33:06,600 --> 00:33:08,160
I've warned you many times.

655
00:33:08,640 --> 00:33:10,350
Your materials and workmanship

656
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:11,710
are substandard,

657
00:33:11,920 --> 00:33:13,390
and your contractor isn't honest either.

658
00:33:13,990 --> 00:33:15,960
The fact that I waited this long to change contractors

659
00:33:16,030 --> 00:33:17,280
is already doing you a favour.

660
00:33:17,280 --> 00:33:18,800
You just want to destroy my livelihood!

661
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:19,990
Save your excuses!

662
00:33:20,390 --> 00:33:21,510
Times have changed.

663
00:33:22,190 --> 00:33:23,640
When you run a legitimate business,

664
00:33:23,640 --> 00:33:26,120
people expect you to deal fairly with everyone.

665
00:33:26,390 --> 00:33:27,640
You can't just force a deal.

666
00:33:28,280 --> 00:33:29,800
If you can't adapt to the times,

667
00:33:30,030 --> 00:33:31,800
you'd better find another way to make a living.

668
00:33:38,510 --> 00:33:39,320
Hui!

669
00:33:42,600 --> 00:33:45,550
You made a bit of money in real estate, and now you think you're something?

670
00:33:45,550 --> 00:33:46,550
Listen carefully.

671
00:33:46,870 --> 00:33:49,710
If we hadn't risked our lives for the gang,

672
00:33:49,830 --> 00:33:50,960
would you be where you are today?

673
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:52,080
As long as you're alive,

674
00:33:52,190 --> 00:33:54,080
you're not leaving us behind!

675
00:33:55,030 --> 00:33:56,160
Don't even think about it!

676
00:33:57,120 --> 00:33:58,480
Don't you dare!

677
00:34:02,550 --> 00:34:03,670
Drop dead!

678
00:34:06,090 --> 00:34:09,540
I watched my dad die right in front of me.

679
00:34:14,440 --> 00:34:16,440
Don't look at me like that.

680
00:34:19,670 --> 00:34:22,510
In fact, my mum has always been loyal to her people.

681
00:34:23,390 --> 00:34:26,550
After all, she and those old friends have been through life and death together.

682
00:34:30,350 --> 00:34:32,870
All I can do is turn a blind eye.

683
00:34:34,190 --> 00:34:35,350
As long as they make their money,

684
00:34:36,830 --> 00:34:37,920
stay out of trouble,

685
00:34:37,920 --> 00:34:39,190
and don't interfere with Tin Ping's business,

686
00:34:39,830 --> 00:34:41,870
I pretend nothing's happening.

687
00:34:43,800 --> 00:34:45,640
How much does your brother know?

688
00:34:46,160 --> 00:34:47,870
My brother was still young back then.

689
00:34:47,870 --> 00:34:48,600
He doesn't remember much.

690
00:34:55,480 --> 00:34:57,190
Once the older generation is gone,

691
00:34:57,640 --> 00:34:59,080
I won't have my hands tied anymore.

692
00:35:06,230 --> 00:35:07,030
Okay.

693
00:35:08,990 --> 00:35:09,800
Okay?

694
00:35:13,030 --> 00:35:14,030
Okay.

695
00:35:23,350 --> 00:35:24,160
Actually,

696
00:35:24,960 --> 00:35:26,190
the way you're feeling right now

697
00:35:26,990 --> 00:35:29,350
is exactly how I felt when I found out you were a police officer.

698
00:35:29,800 --> 00:35:30,600
What?

699
00:35:30,600 --> 00:35:32,190
Are you raking up the past now?

700
00:35:32,190 --> 00:35:33,670
I'm saying I know how you feel.

701
00:35:35,030 --> 00:35:35,960
Happy now?

702
00:35:40,190 --> 00:35:43,280
From now on, you have to tell me if anything happens.

703
00:35:44,080 --> 00:35:44,990
Stop hiding things from me.

704
00:35:45,670 --> 00:35:46,550
Can you do that?

705
00:35:55,350 --> 00:35:56,160
Got it.

706
00:36:18,160 --> 00:36:18,960
Hey, sirs.

707
00:36:19,320 --> 00:36:20,160
We're closing up.

708
00:36:24,230 --> 00:36:25,190
Our clothes!

709
00:36:56,290 --> 00:37:16,640
[Episode 4]
[This story is fictional. Any resemblance is entirely coincidental.]
